# Ignore rules scoped to the slatwall-ts/ subtree. Git applies every pattern below
# relative to THIS directory, so nothing here can reach — or is duplicated from — the
# legacy CFML tree.
#
# That scoping is the reason the file exists. The repository-root .gitignore covers the
# legacy application in 15 entries and not one of them covers node_modules, dist or
# coverage; closing that gap here instead of there keeps the root file, and the whole
# CFML tree, byte-for-byte unchanged, so this port stays a single additive diff
# (AAP 0.4.1.1 / TR-6; 0.5.6.2 lists the root .gitignore as "explicitly not updated").
#
# The list is deliberately short: every entry names an artifact this subtree actually
# produces, and speculative boilerplate is omitted rather than copied in (AAP 0.7.3
# standard 9, guideline 0.8.2/1). The three directory names are shared with
# tsconfig.json "exclude", tsconfig.build.json "outDir" and "exclude",
# eslint.config.mjs "ignores", jest.config.ts "coverageDirectory" and
# "testPathIgnorePatterns", and the output directory in build/esbuild.mjs. All six must
# keep saying the same three words, or a build product ends up tracked.

# Installed dependency tree, materialised by `npm ci` from package-lock.json. The
# lockfile itself is deliberately NOT ignored: a committed lockfile is what makes the
# exact-version resolution reproducible (AAP 0.7.3 standard 5).
node_modules/

# Compiled and bundled output. Both routes to an artifact emit here — `tsc -p
# tsconfig.build.json` (outDir "dist") and `node build/esbuild.mjs` (bundle, source maps
# and metafile.json) — and build products are never committed.
dist/

# Jest coverage reports (jest.config.ts, coverageDirectory: 'coverage').
coverage/

# A real .env is a local developer convenience that may hold live database credentials,
# so it never enters git; configuration reaches the service through the environment and
# no credential is hardcoded (AAP 0.8.3.9). The pattern is the exact filename and not a
# wildcard, so the required, committed .env.example — variable names only, no values —
# is never swallowed.
.env
